1]Explain indetail about ExceptionHandling ?

	->Exception handling in java is a powerful mechanism to handle runtime errors and ensuring the normal flow
	of the application is called as Exception handling.
	->An exception is an event that disrupts the normal flow of the program and it is an object that is thrown
	at runtime when an error occurs,Exceptions can be caused by various reasons such as invalid input,device
	failures,loss of network connection or code errors
	->Their are 2 types of exceptions:-
		i)checked exception (compile time exceptions)
		ii)unchecked exception (run time exceptions)
		
Checked Exception:-
===================
	->The exceptions which are checked by the compiler wheather the programmer is handling or not for smooth
	execution of program during runtime is called as checked exception
	->checked exceptions should be handled by the programmer
	
	few examples: 
		i)IOexception : This exception occurs when an IO Operation fails or interupted
		ii)FileNotFoundException : This exception occurs when iam trying to read the file which was not found
		iii)SQLException : This exception provides the information regarding the database access errors
		
	->We can also create our own custom checked exception by extending the Exception class

Unchecked Exception:-
=====================
	->The exceptions which are not checked by the compiler wheather the programmer is handling or not is
	called as unchecked exception
	
	few examples:
		i)ArithematicException : This exception occurs when an exceptional arithematic condition has occured
		such as division by zero.
		ii)NullPointerException : This exception occurs when an application attempts to use null in a case
		where an object is required
		iii)ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException : This exception is thrown to indicate that an array has been
		accessed with illegal index
		iv)illegalArgumentException: This exception is thrown to indicate that a method has been accessed with
		illegal argument.
	->We can also create our own custom unchecked exception by extending the RuntimeException class

->In Exception handling thier are 5 keywords:-
	1]try-block: The block of code where an exception might occurs
	2]catch-block : The block of code that handles the exception
	3]finally-block : The block of code that is executed regardless wheather an exception occurs or not
	4]throw : is used to explicitly throw an exception from a method or block of code.
	5]throws : is used with method signature to declare a exception,that a method can throw an exception
	
	throws cannot handle the exception,it deligades the exception to its method caller
	To handle exceptions in java we need to use only try-catch blocks
	
	
->we can use this try-catch-finally blocks in different combinations
	i)try-catch
	ii)try-finally
	iii)try-catch-finally
	iv)try- with multiple catch blocks
	v]try with resource
	
	
->Difference between Error and Exception ?

	1]An Exception is an event that disrupts the normal of the program
	2]It usually happens inside the program logic or external condition
	3]Exception is coming from java.lang.Exception class
	4]Programmer need to handle the exception
	
	Example:ArithematicException,SQLException,NullPointerException.
	
	1]Error indicates a serious problem that caused the outside the control of a program
	2]Error is coming from java.lang.Error class
	3]Errors are usually caused by JVM or system components but not with the program logic
	
	Example:OutOfMemoryError,StackOverFlowError
	
	Exception handling hierarchy
	============================
		java.lang.Object
    			|
    			└── java.lang.Throwable
           	 │
            	 ├── java.lang.Exception
            	 │     │
            	 │     ├── java.lang.RuntimeException (Base of ALL Unchecked Exceptions)
            	 │     │     ├── ArithmeticException
            	 │     │     ├── NullPointerException
            	 │     │     ├── ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
            	 │     │     └── IllegalArgumentException
            	 │     │
            	 │     └── Direct Subclasses (Checked / Compile-Time Exceptions)
            	 │           ├── IOException
            	 │           │     └── FileNotFoundException
            	 │           └── SQLException
            	 │
            	 └── java.lang.Error (JVM / System Faults - Unchecked)
                  ├── OutOfMemoryError
                  └── StackOverflowError